                "A transformer changes the voltage of electricity. Power leaves a plant, is stepped up to very high voltage to travel long distances with little loss, and is stepped down in stages at substations until it reaches homes and factories. Each step needs a transformer, and the higher the voltage, the fewer companies are allowed to make it. **The market is modest in money but large in units.** Mordor Intelligence puts India's transformer market at about US$3.25bn in 2026, growing about 8% a year to US$4.82bn by 2031, with distribution transformers about 59% of it. In physical terms, India added 113,013 MVA of 220 kV-and-above transformation in FY26, 90% of the CEA's target, and the FY27 target is 40% higher. **My view: demand for FY27–FY29 is secure; the open questions are who can deliver it, and at what margin.**",
